@page "/docs/tools/pages"

@* izzy add page and izzy add razor (src/IzzyBlazor.Cli/Pages.cs; catalog/page, catalog/razor): the file, the route,
   the render mode, the layout, the nav link, the @using a new folder needs, and what each refuses. Free, no account. *@

<ArticlePage Section="tools" Slug="pages">
    <Lead>
        <Code>izzy add page</Code> adds a new page to your app with its route, its title and a container to start
        in. <Code>izzy add razor</Code> adds a component with no route, for a part you use on several pages.
        Neither needs an account. For a page that lists and edits a model's records, see
        <Anchor Href="docs/tools/crud">CRUD pages</Anchor>.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">Add a page</Heading>
        <TextBlock>Run it in your app's folder with the page's name:</TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="bash">izzy add page --name MonthlyReports --nav</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            izzy writes <Code>Components/Pages/MonthlyReports.razor</Code> at the address
            <Code>/monthly-reports</Code>, titled "Monthly reports". With <Code>--nav</Code>, it adds a link to the
            page in the app's nav.
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor" Title="Components/Pages/MonthlyReports.razor">@PageFile</Code>
        <Table Items="PageOptions" Caption="Options of izzy add page" Size="ControlSize.Sm" Class="site-params" Bordered="false">
            <Columns>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Option" Width="Length.Rem(14)"><code>@context!.Name</code></TemplateColumn>
                <TemplateColumn Title="What it does">@context!.Text</TemplateColumn>
            </Columns>
        </Table>
        <TextBlock>
            izzy doesn't replace a page. When the file is already there, or another page has the route, it stops
            and names the file.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Render mode</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            A page is static unless you say otherwise: its C# runs on the server once for each request.
            <Code>--mode server</Code> writes <Code>@@rendermode InteractiveServer</Code> on the page.
            <Code>--mode webassembly</Code> and <Code>--mode auto</Code> put the page in the app's
            <Code>.Client</Code> project, where it runs in the browser. In an app whose pages are all interactive,
            the page says nothing and takes the app's mode. See
            <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">Render modes</Anchor>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Add a component</Heading>
        <Code Block Language="bash">izzy add razor --name OrderSummary --folder Components/Shared</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            izzy writes <Code>Components/Shared/OrderSummary.razor</Code>, an empty component to fill in. When the
            folder is new, it adds the folder's <Code>@@using</Code> line to <Code>_Imports.razor</Code>, so every
            page can write <Code>&lt;OrderSummary /&gt;</Code>. Without <Code>--folder</Code>, the file goes in
            <Code>Components</Code>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">See the change first</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Both commands take <Code>--dry-run</Code>, <Code>--diff</Code> and <Code>--json</Code>. See
            <Anchor Href="docs/tools/changes">Previewing changes</Anchor>.
        </TextBlock>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private sealed record Row(string Name, string Text);

    private const string PageFile = """
        @page "/monthly-reports"

        <PageTitle>Monthly reports</PageTitle>

        <Container Size="ContainerSize.Md" Align="ContainerAlign.Start" Gutters="false">
            <Column Gap="new() { Base = 6, Md = 8 }">
                <PageHeader Title="Monthly reports" />
            </Column>
        </Container>
        """;

    private static readonly Row[] PageOptions =
    [
        new("--name <Name>", "The component's name and its file. Its words are the page's title."),
        new("--route <path>", "The page's address, such as reports or reports/{year:int}. Without it, the name in kebab case."),
        new("--folder <folder>", "The folder the file goes in, from the project's folder. Without it, Components/Pages."),
        new("--mode Static", "Where the page's C# runs: Static, Server, WebAssembly or Auto."),
        new("--layout <Layout>", "The layout component, such as EmptyLayout, when the page doesn't use the app's default."),
        new("--nav", "Adds a link to the page in the app's nav."),
        new("--project <path>", "The app's project, when it isn't the folder you run izzy in."),
    ];
}
